 it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{x} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{(-2)} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362800 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362801 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362802 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362803 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362804 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362801 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362799 1080 #uuid "e02b7c91-76ce-53ed-b342-163951d05f8f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362800 1081 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362800 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362800 1084 #uuid "60b15d99-5f73-5d71-a0a0-49f9be9df65d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362801 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362801 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362801 1084 #uuid "3cefcde2-3aa5-51a2-8f0c-24c6172e631c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362802 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362802 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362802 1084 #uuid "243ba24f-c088-5741-b1dc-797cc0c88bb6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362803 1081 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362803 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362803 1084 #uuid "3ab4b002-dd36-598f-8102-522b7e368735" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362804 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362804 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362804 1084 #uuid "4a73df82-8e85-5bb1-90fc-89e5be58e836" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362806 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1069 "q-143108" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1071 "At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the derivative ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **inversely** proportional to the distance from $P$ to the origin. What differential equation describes this curve?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1072 #uuid "0fa1a884-5f7e-5470-a5fd-08ae0d0d0b0f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362805 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the **derivative** ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **inversely proportional** to the **distance from $P$ to the origin**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The *distance from $P(x,y)$ to the origin* is given by $\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$\n\n- Since the *derivative* is *inversely proportional* to the distance from $P$ to the origin, we have \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=k\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant.\n\nSo, our differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362806 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362807 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362806 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362808 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362806 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362809 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362806 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362810 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362806 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362811