592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1071 "![](images/5f/5f91cc8b30f9b764021cd84c374a328c7ffb1287a9f0dc6a211a3fadfac2fdbd.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u{v}^{2},\\,y={u}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$*" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1072 #uuid "e4de9b2d-c42a-5fe3-94b3-1b2caac795c3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1074 "We're told that $T$ has no critical points in the interior of $Δ.$ So, to map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we transform each side of $Δ$ separately:\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{1},$ where we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u({0}^{2}),\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,{u}^{2}), & 0\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a vertical line segment traversed from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(0,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{2}.$ Here, we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(1{v}^{2},\\,{1}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =({v}^{2},\\,1), & 0\\le v\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment traversed from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{3}.$ Here, we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u({1}^{2}),\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(u,\\,{u}^{2}), & 1\\ge u\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola traversed from the point $(1,1)$ to the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Consider the image of the side ${S}_{4}.$ Here, we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) &  \\\\  & =(u{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0{v}^{2},\\,{0}^{2}) &  \\\\  & =(0,\\,0), & 1\\ge v\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThis is the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nDrawing the images of the sides of our square, we obtain the following image of $Δ:$\n\n![](images/64/648fa48df1bd648d9fbf48efc966698228416ad9bf3a0f69045031e955601d61.png)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362917 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362918 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362919 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362920 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362921 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362919 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1080 #uuid "515b035c-875d-5a93-a2bf-bdd77d9642fd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362917 1081 "images/72/72e271d6a2282fdf7cdf852308f569de848b8bdc71935e1487969f9ea7ac3eb0.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362917 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362917 1084 #uuid "3bd9f9d6-0406-5b60-bf3c-c7fb79ebaf40" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362918 1081 "images/e3/e3cfcf4c6cd7bcc8298a7e3d8c76f4add3f61689cecc1dacb9fa8a48db5a042b.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362918 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362918 1084 #uuid "b9c07d75-8dc0-5472-b4ee-118ce7ee6da5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362919 1081 "images/64/648fa48df1bd648d9fbf48efc966698228416ad9bf3a0f69045031e955601d61.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362919 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362919 1084 #uuid "4157d539-f77d-5f54-8554-c73457ce6de7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362920 1081 "images/3b/3ba341827d95d261f8def4462a11282051b3605795459343441f9f35284faf33.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362920 1084 #uuid "c5415f6b-51be-511e-8dcf-7bc985ea09e4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362921 1081 "images/0f/0fd03370c63540a8dc9336305bbf917239f02afce2f73371715d6489eee31c9b.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362921 1084 #uuid "fd8fcb79-14f8-54fd-8a6b-4be84dab14e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362923 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1069 "q-160897" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1071 "Using the change of variables $u=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}$ and $v=xy,$ evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\,dx\\,dy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4{x}^{2},\\,1\\le xy\\le 5}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1072 #uuid "c98b0d83-24f7-5020-a2b4-fd331038c974" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362922 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,v=xy\n$$\n\n \ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows::\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,1\\le v\\le 5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}} & \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & \\text{ }\\text{ }x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}=-\\frac{1}{3u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}v|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}v\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{v}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}v[{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}v[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{1}^{4}]dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{5}v\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}\\cdot (25-1) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362924 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362925 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362926 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362927 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362928 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362928 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362923 1080 #uuid "d8dfde2a-78d4-5f4f-9dd7-f750b4f43d5c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362924 1081 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362924 1084 #uuid "e344f475-3668-5c1f-9b88-0fa12f4ef4de" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362925 1081 "\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362925 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362925 1084 #uuid "17a3824c-bebc-5701-8d19-9114502785b4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362926 1081 "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362926 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362926 1084 #uuid "bf4f6312-74e7-571d-b7fe-be323a268da2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362927 1081 "6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362927 1084 #uuid "22d2eda0-0d96-5f44-84d6-338243168c0b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362928 1081 "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362928 1084 #uuid "fcec1dbc-cba7-5afe-82ab-ccf5f65b004f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362930 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1069 "q-160901" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1071 "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi (x+y))\\,dxdy,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the quadrilateral region with vertices $(0,0),$ $(1,-1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(0,1).$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1072 #uuid "c887f553-5496-5423-9167-1a0440f8386c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362929 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe integrand\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi (x+y))\n$$\n\nsuggests that we use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x,\\,v=x+y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nThe vertices of our domain $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(0,0) & =(0,0+0) \\\\  & =(0,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(1,-1) & =(1,1+(-1)) \\\\  & =(1,0) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(1,0) & =(1,1+0) \\\\  & =(1,1) \\\\ {T}^{-1}(0,1) & =(0,0+1) \\\\  & =(0,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\n![](images/5b/5be3ed729654d60b6084200334086b35f093e461bfa2f0eb9d8f0c323f007fb3.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=1\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi (x+y))\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi v)\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi v)\\,|1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi v)\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi v)}{\\pi }]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362931 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362932 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362933 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362934 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362935 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362935 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362930 1080 #uuid "95107d27-68cf-5739-8e44-f4226a672f34" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362931 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362931 1084 #uuid "790e8e07-7e51-507f-8184-c6e269fb8de8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362932 1081 "\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362932 1084 #uuid "e4fff2f8-8d95-5435-b189-10210d784148" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362933 1081 "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362933 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362933 1084 #uuid "f14b4067-73c1-5f25-863f-0a6233383ceb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362934 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362934 1084 #uuid "39736917-e30f-55c3-8963-53bb38f33eca" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362935 1081 "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362935 1083 #edb/ref 1759218604