bian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=-1\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2x-y){e}^{(2x-y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,|-1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}v{e}^{{v}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{v}^{2}}]}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[u]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}-e)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362966 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362967 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362968 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362969 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362970 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362966 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362965 1080 #uuid "f332d7f0-0c51-591d-8a07-616530eb39fa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362966 1081 "{e}^{4}-