197 1081 "6\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363197 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363197 1084 #uuid "ae328f95-387f-55bc-b6b1-78da1a0e6c8b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363198 1081 "2\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363198 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363198 1084 #uuid "9829f33d-f493-59a1-b8be-a91cbaec38dc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363200 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1069 "q-162570" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1071 "![](images/98/9861e9edc3c7517af6fd912046f62ec04a6e478942c3017ed9903e8b366130c2.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=⟨1-2x,\\,5y-3{z}^{2},\\,{x}^{3}-{y}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by the bounding region of a right circular cylinder of height $2$ whose base is a circle of radius $3$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Given that $S$ is positively (outward) oriented, use the divergence theorem to find the flux of $F$ through $S.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1072 #uuid "139943e3-1c42-5e1e-8135-8c3ce7b2dffc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363199 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1-2x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5y-3{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2+5+0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid cylinder enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & =3{∭}_{R}\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\text{Volume}(R) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =54\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363201 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363202 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363203 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363204 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363205 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363202 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363200 1080 #uuid "9accbfc9-5746-540c-8cdb-b27e56facfc9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363201 1081 "32\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363201 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363201 1084 #uuid "9dedb4d6-dae2-543b-80b2-9ccef9fa5a88" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363202 1081 "54\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363202 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363202 1084 #uuid "8eabaa4a-a54f-5ddc-885b-ce8690b34285" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363203 1081 "64\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363203 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363203 1084 #uuid "896566d9-4a61-5d61-b4f4-4aa45c0939f5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363204 1081 "27\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363204 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363204 1084 #uuid "4dc850a0-843d-56eb-abc2-2419b6e13be9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363205 1081 "48\\pi " 