87 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1071 "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x+4{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{2}}$ given that the area of the region is $\\frac{9}{4}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1072 #uuid "2b5e586b-c2dc-540a-a0ad-a2a21d4d395f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363247 1074 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{9}{4})}{∬}_{D}x+4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{x/2}x+4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[xy+\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]_{y=0}^{y=x/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}]_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{3}^{4}}{24}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{4\\cdot {3}^{3}+{3}^{4}}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{63}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363249 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363250 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363251 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363252 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363253 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363249 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363248 1080 #uuid "fdd89614-6ef6-5ce5-9070-36f61efa21d2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363249 1081 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363249 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363249 1084 #uuid "a1ebfe9c-56c5-580b-b413-f8c97a0a371a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363250 1081 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363250 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363250 1084 #uuid "6f62a775-9c4b-543c-abf0-e5519e4ed2c4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1081 "4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363251 1084 #uuid "e9502132-04e2-51a9-815f-b12655963eef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1081 "5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363252 1084 #uuid "54086852-a949-5220-87bd-7465711fbbe1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1081 "\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363253 1084 #uuid "aa8ec75e-85f4-516d-aefe-94d64aad2131" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363255 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1069 "q-163258" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1071 "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ on the disk of radius $6$ centered at the origin." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1072 #uuid "75bad8c5-dff2-5d67-88eb-d6d0bf7d0cd9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363254 1074 "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}=36\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 6,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{6}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,{[\\frac{{r}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(\\frac{{6}^{3}}{3}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =72{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =72[\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =72(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =144\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{36\\pi }\\cdot 144\\pi =4.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363256 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363257 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363258 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363259 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363260 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363258 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363255 1080 #uuid "bc7f9b80-4da3-54b1-86b1-061f4bb5871e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363256 1081 "4\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363256 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363256 1084 #uuid "4e5aab61-e10d-5d70-b0f7-6e6729d9b55e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363257 1081 "6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363257 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363257 1084 #uuid "671de7df-a317-5899-8601-99987364cb06" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363258 1081 "4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363258 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363258 1084 #uuid "0ee5c801-cb1c-52e8-8d0b-fe1360b04e31" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363259 1081 "6\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363259 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363259 1084 #uuid "585fed5e-2b0e-5b99-8a78-50744708f0ac" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363260 1081 "24" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363260 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363260 1084 #uuid "0212216e-d531-5268-a6e6-ce76d6ad38d3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363262 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1069 "q-168126" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1071 "![](images/e0/e07ec409a9a25fbd444dc9548d69972c37bcb0112b9de220c463299666216393.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1072 #uuid "e8c81957-743a-520c-a208-3d03ce4b0147" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363261 1074 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=y+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,y=x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nThe function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/59/599aad21fec8f1c43c674063c34eaffa8e73857dd35cac8caba0d4a593c6a3f8.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we have $x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le y\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le y\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363263 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363264 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363265 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363266 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363267 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363264 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363262 1080 #uuid "a32cd938-fa8a-540f-8c36-fa170a143885" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363263 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le y\\le \\operatorname{arccos}⁡x}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363263 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585