86363944 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363955 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363944 1069 "q-337751" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363944 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363944 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-3y=g(x).\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-3x}:$According to the method of variation of parameters, we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}={u}_{1}(x),{u}_{2}={u}_{2}(x),$ that satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expressions $y={y}_{p}$ and ${y}^{′}={y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation yields the following relationship between ${u}_{1}^{′},{u}_{2}^{′},$ and $g(x):$\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363944 1072 #uuid "f89bf15e-170f-57b4-987e-95e2136f7222" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363944 1074 "Given a second-order linear inhomogeneous differential equation, the variation of parameters method requires that we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}(x)+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}(x)\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}.\n$$\n\nHere, ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly independent solutions of the corresponding homogeneous equation, and ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nIn this case, we're told that the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}={e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our expression for ${y}_{p},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}={u}_{1}{e}^{x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}({e}^{x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-3x})^{′}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y={y}_{p}$ and ${y}^{′}={y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-3y & =g(x) \\\\ ({y}_{p}^{′})^{′}+2{y}_{p}^{′}-3{y}_{p} & =g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing our expressions for ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({u}_{1}({e}^{x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-3x})^{′})}^{′}+2({u}_{1}({e}^{x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-3x})^{′})-3({u}_{1}{e}^{x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x}) & =g(x) \\\\ {({u}_{1}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x})}^{′}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{x}-6{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x}-3{u}_{1}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x} & =g(x) \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{x}+{u}_{1}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-3x}+9{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{x}-6{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x}-3{u}_{1}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}{e}^{-3x} & =g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group all terms proportional to ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}{{({e}^{x}+2{e}^{x}-3{e}^{x})}_{⏟}}_{0}+{u}_{2}{{(9{e}^{-3x}-6{e}^{-3x}-3{e}^{-3x})}_{⏟}}_{0}+{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-3x}=g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the expressions in parentheses are both zero. Therefore, the equation reduces to\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{x}-3{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-3x}=g(x).\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363946 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363947 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363948 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363949 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1077 "field-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363947 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363945 1080 #uuid "2daf61ca-2864-5046-9a57-41a4be211613" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363946 1081 "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-3x}={g}^{′}(x)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363946 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [175