ian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\text{ }\\text{ }1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3(x+y)^{2}\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}3{u}^{2}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}3{u}^{2}|\\frac{1}{2}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{u}^{2}\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364524 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364525 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364526 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364528 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364523 1080 #uuid "da395623-3256-578e-8977-74807708542d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1081 "6{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{u}^{2}\\,dv\\,du" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364524 1084 #uuid "0b519e