 position $x$ of the particle at time $t\\ge 1.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364543 1072 #uuid "02b3d021-7593-5ac9-9257-81d284bac79e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364543 1074 "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(1)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\frac{1}{1}+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=-\\frac{1}{t}+1.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{t}+1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(1)=4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1+K \\\\ 4 & =-0+1+K \\\\ K & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t+3.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364545 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364546 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364547 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364548 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364549 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364548 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364544 1080 #uuid "9a2c2e46-526b-5812-b102-34de4caa62b4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364545 1081 "x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2" 13194139533445 1759218604558